\description{
Functions to assign amplicon sequence variants (ASVs) to a curated reference
database using either exact sequence matching or BLASTn alignment.
\itemize{
\item \code{rb_assign_edna()}: Main wrapper for taxonomic assignment.
\item \code{rb_assign_blastn()}: Runs BLASTn against a reference database.
\item \code{rb_exact_hits()}: Finds exact sequence matches in the reference.
\item \code{rb_score_assignments()}: Resolves and scores assignment hits, handling ties.
\item \code{rb_parse_blast_tabular()}: Parses standard BLAST tabular output.
\item \code{rb_build_species_matrix()}: Aggregates ASV assignments into a species-by-sample matrix.
\item \code{rb_read_fasta()}: Reads a FASTA file into a data frame (used internally for ASV input).
}
}
\details{
When \code{method = "blastn"}, BLAST+ must be installed and \code{blastn} and \code{makeblastdb} must be available on the system path.

The assignment pipeline utilizes advanced alignment mettrics to prevent common BLAST biases. It calculates subject coverage (\code{scovs}), combined coverage (\code{ccovs} = sqrt(qcov * scovs)), and bitscore per base (\code{bitscore_pb}). Hits are ranked using a robust hierarchy: \code{-bitscore}, \code{-bitscore_pb}, \code{evalue}, \code{-ccovs}, \code{-pident}.

The \code{assignment_status} column classifies the result:
\itemize{
\item \code{"unique"}: A single best species match.
\item \code{"ambiguous"}: Multiple species tied, but with slight metric variations.
\item \code{"check_full_tie"}: Multiple species tied with perfectly identical top metrics across the board, requiring manual biogeographical or taxonomic curation.
\item \code{"no_match"}: No hits passed the coverage/identity filters.
}

For ties, the \code{tie_taxa} column contains a pipe-separated (\code{|}) string of the tied species names (e.g., \code{"Species A|Species B"}). If there is no tie, this column is \code{NA}.
}
